    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Job’s Reply to Eliphaz"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then Job answered:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I have heard many things like these.",
          "You are all miserable comforters."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Is there no end to your empty , words?",
          "What provokes you that you continue testifying?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If you were in my place I could also talk like you.",
          "I could string words together against you",
          "and shake my head at you."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Instead, I would encourage you with my mouth,",
          "and the consolation from my lips would bring relief."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If I speak, my suffering is not relieved,",
          "and if I hold back, does any of it leave me?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Surely he has now exhausted me.",
          "You have devastated my entire family."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have shriveled me up #— #it has become a witness;",
          "my frailty rises up against me and testifies to my face."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "His anger tears at me, and he harasses me.",
          "He gnashes his teeth at me.",
          "My enemy pierces me with his eyes."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They open their mouths against me",
          "and strike my cheeks with contempt;",
          "they join themselves together against me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God hands me over to the unjust;",
          "he throws me to the wicked."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I was at ease, but he shattered me;",
          "he seized me by the scruff of the neck",
          "and smashed me to pieces.",
          "He set me up as his target;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "his archers surround me.",
          "He pierces my kidneys without mercy",
          "and pours my bile on the ground."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He breaks through my defenses again and again;",
          "he charges at me like a warrior."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I have sewn sackcloth over my skin;",
          "I have buried my strength in the dust."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My face has grown red with weeping,",
          "and darkness covers my eyes,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "although my hands are free from violence",
          "and my prayer is pure."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Earth, do not cover my blood;",
          "may my cry for help find no resting place."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Even now my witness is in heaven,",
          "and my advocate is in the heights!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My friends scoff at me",
          "as I weep before God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I wish that someone might argue for a man with God",
          "just as anyone would for a friend."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For only a few years will pass",
          "before I go the way of no return."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
